## SEVERITY / VERDICT (decided HERE; apply it, do not re-argue it)
*Blocker:* a path beyond the three; any product byte changed (any blob of `web/src` other than `HpLogo.test.tsx`, any protected file of Check 1); a new row RED at the unmutated head; the new spec RED at the unmutated head on YOUR block (after a rerun alone twice); the head moved (a verdict is valid only at the head it ran on); a failing web suite, lint, typecheck, build or shard-check step at the head after it is re-run alone twice and not red at base; a reproduced timing red (3 of 3 alone at the head, not at base); a NEW CodeQL alert at or above the ruleset's thresholds on the changed lines; a secret in the diff, the message or the evidence; a person's name, decision-card id or `B###` token in an added line or the commit message; a request to any origin other than your loopback ports; a run of yours that binds 3100, 3597, 3598 or 3599; a merge that would deploy. *Major (class "a pinned row that does not turn red under the defect it names, or turns red for another reason"):* a ticket-shape plant (p1 to p4) that the NEW unit row leaves GREEN; the NEW spec GREEN under p1 at 1440x900; p5 GREEN under BOTH the unit arm and the spec; a row that turns red for a reason other than its title; a builder claim contradicted by measurement with a verdict consequence (the suite does not reproduce as 3036 to 3039, the shard does not read 130 to 134); a REFUSE on the third `webServer` entry (class "CI configuration that starts a process the shard does not use"); a path shared with another open PR; a failing required check. *Minor/Note:* p5 or p6 or p7 GREEN in the unit arm only while the spec is RED (layered design; ticket text for the unit arm); p2 GREEN in the spec at 390x844 (by design); the header and sign-in rows' raw-token paint check (the builder's "Outside the lane" note; ticket text for a follow-up); a stale local figure in the PR body; the commit subject and PR title differing; the Co-Authored-By trailer; unsigned commit; the `next start` standalone warning; CodeQL PENDING